# Frontend documentation work

When editing `docs/frontend-standards.md` or `docs/frontend-patterns.md`:

- Keep the docs Nexus-specific, not inherited from another product
- Reference real routes, pages, components, and patterns from the active frontend root (`Nexus.Dashboard/`, `Refactor/web/`, or future `web/`)
- Keep `frontend-standards.md` as constitution (must / never)
- Keep `frontend-patterns.md` as recipes and decision trees
- When a reusable UI pattern becomes canonical, add it to `frontend-patterns.md` in the same change
- Do not add references to nonexistent docs, routes, products, or UI surfaces
